  "question": "Find the area bounded by the parabola $y = x^2$, the line $y = 2x$, and the $x$-axis.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Intersection points from $x^2=2x$ give $x=0,2$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{0}^{2}(2x-x^2)dx$.<br /><br />$=[x^2-\\frac{x^3}{3}]_{0}^{2}=4-\\frac{8}{3}=\\frac{4}{3}$.<br /><br />Thus area is $\\dfrac{4}{3}$ square units.",
